==========================================================
G. SUPERVISION WORKFLOW
==========================================================

Use an explicit state-based workflow.

Proposed cycle states:

draft
scheduled
observed
followup
reflected
completed

Workflow:

1. Teacher creates a new supervision cycle.
2. Teacher completes and submits Form A.
3. Principal reviews the submission.
4. Principal approves the observation schedule.
5. Principal observes classroom practice and completes Form B.
6. Principal publishes observation feedback.
7. Teacher reads the observation results.
8. Teacher completes Form C.
9. Principal reviews the follow-up plan.
10. Teacher implements the agreed improvement.
11. Teacher completes Form D.
12. Principal reviews the reflection.
13. Principal finalizes the supervision cycle.
14. The completed cycle becomes a permanent, read-only internal archive.

Do not unlock a later stage before prerequisites are completed.

Use database-backed workflow state, not localStorage status.

The system must display the next required action to each user.

Provide controlled revision requests for future implementation, but never permit unauthorized overwriting of finalized records.

